    "turn_text": "There are stories I read later about Frank Untenmeyer, a professor there, helping out students. I was in a position where I had to largely put myself through undergraduate graduate school and law school. And in a particularly difficult time, for a whole lot of reasons, I went to meet him about a paper I was writing, and there was a reception had just been completed afterwards, you know, before I went to see him. And so I went over there outside his office and I picked an apple off the table and went in to see him. Someone called to complain to him that I had taken food and he said, well, maybe he was hungry. Have you been hungry? Because starving college student, right? And while I sat there, he wrote me a check and said, pay me back when you can. Bobby Rush went there too and years Congressman Bobby Rush yeah and Bobby Rush said something I wish I had thought of first he said it so well Roosevelt was a very special place to go not just because of the education but because of the students you were you were surrounded by he said Roosevelt loved me before I loved Roosevelt it was an amazing experience and",
